## The field views: a second file

The field views come as a second file, `kisi-advanced.html` (about 9.5 MB), which must be in the same folder as
`kisi.html`. This is a deliberate trade-off: `kisi.html` stays small (about 3.8 MB) and quick to open, and the full-wave 2D
solver and the 3D view load only when "Fields…" is used. The field page's interface (the 2D page from the js_2d_fields
fork, the 3D view) may be unified with kisi's viewer and optimised in a future release.

## Known limits of the field views

* 3D view: the dielectric loss is right at f_loss (the geometric mean of the chosen field frequencies) only; at other
  frequencies of the broadband S-parameters it is an estimate (too high below f_loss, too low above).
* 3D view: the step and time estimate before a run is too low for pad-port cases at BGA fan-outs (a fan-out on the
  standard mesh: about 42 s estimated, 447 s in the browser).
* 3D view: a cut-out has lumped 50 Ω ports (pad ports where a trace ends at a pad) and its feed lines; its
  S-parameters and TDR are not de-embedded.
* The 2D full-wave views and the 3D view need a recent Chromium or Firefox (WebAssembly with SIMD, Web Workers,
  compression streams). Phones and tablets are not refused; the 3D view only warns that they may stop a large run.

## Corresponding source of the field page

`kisi-advanced.html` (the 2D cross-section views, full-wave, and the 3D view of a via) is GPL-3.0 and built by the
release workflow from:

* the fork [{fork_repo_name}]({fork_repo}) of js_2d_fields (original by Henrik Forstén) at commit
  [`{fork_commit_short}`]({fork_repo}/tree/{fork_commit}), with kisi's patches {patches} from
  [`web/advanced/fork-patches/`]({kisi_tree}/web/advanced/fork-patches) of this tag;
* kisi's scripts at this tag: [`tools/fetch_fork.sh`]({kisi_tree}/tools/fetch_fork.sh),
  [`tools/advanced_bundle.py`]({kisi_tree}/tools/advanced_bundle.py), [`web/advanced/`]({kisi_tree}/web/advanced) (the 3D
  view in `web/advanced/fdtd/`) and kisi-sparse ([`crates/kisi-sparse`]({kisi_tree}/crates/kisi-sparse)) in place of the
  original's Eigen solver;
* the 3D solver kisi-fdtd ([`crates/kisi-fdtd`]({kisi_tree}/crates/kisi-fdtd)) of this tag as WebAssembly (feature
  `field-view`, SHA-256 {fdtd_sha});
* the full-wave WebAssembly modules, built by
  [`tools/build_forsten_fullwave.sh`]({kisi_tree}/tools/build_forsten_fullwave.sh) from js_2d_fields
  [`{upstream_rev_short}`](https://github.com/Ttl/js_2d_fields/tree/{upstream_rev}) with its submodules {submodules},
  OpenCASCADE {occt} and the Emscripten SDK {emsdk} – licences in the page's third-party notices (About tab).

SHA-256: {page_hashes}. Versions, commits and the modules' SHA-256: `kisi-advanced.build-info.json`.
